  "notes": "A web derivative of the v0.17 character: the cloth is baked on to a lighter body, the screen shows one cell of the face atlas, and each accessory is its own mesh, named Thingy_Accessory_<id>, so a page can show or hide it. A slot gives what a scene can have with it, and an accessory's `absent` mesh takes its place when it comes off. faces.webp is the same atlas, small, for a page that offers the faces. This is not a printable model.",
